    "io_mode": "function",
    "statement": "Simulate a congestion-aware virtual-adapter write worker with a shared spin-credit reservoir.\n\nDefine `simulate_writes(lengths, outcomes, max_retries, level_cap, spin_limit, initial_credits, credit_cap)`.\n\n`lengths` is a list of packet lengths. A packet is valid exactly when its length is in `[1, 65535]`. Invalid packets make no attempt and change no shared state.\n\n`outcomes` is a run-length encoded chronological list of `(kind, count)` pairs. `kind` is `\"ok\"`, `\"full\"`, or `\"error\"`, and `count` is positive. Every write attempt consumes one outcome. After all runs are exhausted, every later attempt implicitly returns `\"error\"`.\n\nThe worker has a congestion level, initially zero and always in `[0, level_cap]`, and a spin-credit balance, initially `initial_credits` and always in `[0, credit_cap]`. Valid packets are processed in order:\n\n* `\"ok\"` sends the packet, decreases the level by one without going below zero, then adds the packet's length to the credit balance, capped at `credit_cap`.\n* `\"error\"` fails the packet and resets the level to zero. Credits are unchanged.\n* `\"full\"` raises the level by one, capped at `level_cap`. Let `old_level` be the level before this increase and l",
